  status='''\n\nRead-only cold-field integrity evidence is in `20261022-core-cost-cold-row-ownership/`: 293 related module checks pass in each legacy/compact configuration and 68 default checks pass. Each group authenticates every Entity-Map/no-competing-ROW route and absence of legacy owner selectors. Every hot-column locator/presence exactly matches membership. Cold locations are traversed by distinct SlotReference, holding one bounded decoded body per block, with exact owner masks, actual row directories/values, disjoint hot/cold tokens, actual LargeValues and cross-block field totals. Cold fields add no per-field selector, so global old OwnerMap/FieldDirectory/ExtensionDirectory counts still exclude orphan entries. `cold_blocks` counts distinct physical block references and `cold_rows` counts nonempty cold owners; aliases do not inflate physical-block counts.\n\nThe reverse phase checks exact group/membership/hot-column/cold-block locators and slot generations in each current Native physical page, rejecting duplicate/orphan blocks and memberships. Cold owner kind is at offset7 (offset6 is codec); the RAW Edge check prevents confusing codec with namespace. Actual LargeValue references must match owner/media/cold-block generation, followed by manifest/content/actual-directory authentication. Physical reference visitors deliver each reference row once and do not replay exceptions. Correct directories alone do not establish unique physical ownership; both phases are necessary.\n\nThese components feed existing whole-database scanner field-graph calls, but tests still use real pages/indexes with the private candidate descriptor. Whole-database, old-pin/fault/move/retirement acceptance after actual public conversion remains pending. Initial failures are retained: the direct-read fixture now supplies its explicit account; independent LargeValue logical generation is commonly1 and cannot be inferred from metadata epochs. The future-reference fault now explicitly forges a generation newer than the block but no newer than the group, and requires local INVALID_HEADER before an actual-manifest identity mismatch. No allowance/cache/storage-format change, full unit suite or timing benchmark; progress remains90%.\n\n**Production publication remains closed.** Forward/reverse field auditing does not fix the legacy LargeValue ownership iterator\'s omission of cold owners. Next add bounded reachability traversal using stable logical owner/group boundaries, actual reference retention and retirement, then complete conversion and mutation lifecycle. Neither partial marks nor non-exhausted scans grant reclamation authority.\n'''
